{"kind":"artifact","text":"internal/workroom implementation at exact clean pushed head 62df7ab67fd9639f9034fdbf4982b05327694b81 on request/dated-active-cause-v2, fulfilling planner's 2906cb7e under promise 60bdd5ee. It closes the forward reference codex found at 914e3964, which I ratified.\n\nA POSITION APPLIED TO HALF A FACT IS NOT A POSITION. The scope filtered the supersession record by sequence and then resolved its successor bases through the fold's end-of-log index. But the basis is an identifier the signer chose, and an identifier can be pre-signed: a supersession filed before a verdict can name an artifact that only materialises after it, and the successor edge then appears retroactively, minting receipt authority from a fact the reviewer could not have seen. The basis record is now held to the same position as the record that cites it. One local cutoff inside the existing scope, reusing the fold's own index -- no second walker, no duplicated vocabulary, which is what codex asked for.\n\nTHE REGRESSION EXERCISES THE BASIS, NOT THE RECORD. My previous test moved the supersession past the verdict and would have passed with this hole wide open; codex said so and was right, and a regression that cannot fail on the defect is not coverage. The new one keeps the supersession before the verdict and materialises its basis after, and it proves non-vacuity at end-of-log first -- the materialised basis genuinely does become a successor edge, and the completed chain genuinely does rescue the plan -- so position is the only variable left when the receipt is refused.\n\nGATES I RAN AT THIS EXACT HEAD, not taken from the implementing agent's report: gofmt clean; go vet ./... clean; go test -count=1 ./... green across every package; go test -race -count=1 on internal/workroom and internal/app clean; GOOS=windows GOARCH=amd64 go build ./... clean; git diff --check clean; worktree clean; origin equals the head.\n\nMUTATIONS I RAN MYSELF, each one compiling -- a mutation that fails to build proves nothing, and I have made that mistake twice this session -- restoring and confirming a clean tree after each. Deleting the new basis-record cutoff kills TestABasisMaterialisedAfterTheVerdictDoesNotServeAsASuccessorAtIt with 'a basis filed after the verdict completed the chain at it, rescued the condemned plan, and minted receipt authority from a fact the reviewer could not have seen'. Removing 'mode != StalenessTerminal' still kills TestADirectlyRetiredTerminalBasisDoesNotDateByTheCauseItStopped. Changing scope.succeededRetirements() to f.succeededRetirements() at the validateMergeReceiptNow call site still kills TestASuccessionDeclaredAfterTheVerdictDoesNotCondemnThePlanAtIt. None of the three earlier guards was weakened by this change.","body":{"commit":"62df7ab67fd9639f9034fdbf4982b05327694b81","path":"internal/workroom"}}